# The disjoined bound ENFORCES on override (fixed 2026-08-26 by the
# preference admission gate, ADR-004).  This probe used to pin the
# fail-open behaviour of README gap 2: 40 is far above max(24), yet the
# concrete peer replaced the *2 default by KIND alone, was never tested
# against the constrained branch, and the file evaluated with exit 0.
# Now the override must be admitted by an alternative (or equal the
# preferred value), so 40 is the empty disjunction: [aontu/empty],
# exit 1.  An in-range override (e.g. 12) is admitted by the
# constrained branch, and an unset field still generates the default 2.
replicas: *2 | (integer & min(1) & max(24))
replicas: 40
